1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,955
What do these numbers tell us?

2
00:00:01,955 --> 00:00:07,985
Along the direction one, one, the matrix stretches everything by three.

3
00:00:07,985 --> 00:00:12,470
Along one, minus one, it leaves everything alone.

4
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:16,441
Now take any other vector, say two, zero.

5
00:00:16,441 --> 00:00:21,852
We can write it as one copy of the yellow vector plus one copy of the green one.

6
00:00:21,852 --> 00:00:26,970
Apply the matrix: the yellow part triples, the green part stays.

7
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:32,705
Together that gives four, two, exactly what the matrix gives directly.

8
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:39,588
So eigenvectors turn a messy transformation into simple stretching along two directions.

9
00:00:39,588 --> 00:00:46,544
And the area of any shape is scaled by three times one, which is three, the determinant.

